{"catalogue_version":"2026.09.16","hits":[{"doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/api/m2/endpoints/m2-callbacks/04-m2-post-v3-patients-sms-on-notify#m2-callback-api-for-sms-notification-to-patients","id":"hiecm.callback.m2-callback-api-for-sms-notification-to-patients","summary":"ABDM answers the HIP's SMS notification request on the HIP's bridge.","title":"Callback API for SMS Notification to patients","type":"callback"},{"doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/api/m2/endpoints/m2-callbacks/03-m2-post-v3-links-context-on-notify#m2-call-back-api-for-notify-care-context-update","id":"hiecm.callback.m2-call-back-api-for-notify-care-context-update","summary":"ABDM answers a care context update notification on the HIP's bridge.","title":"Call back API for notify care context update","type":"callback"},{"doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/api/m2/endpoints/m2-callbacks/02-m2-post-v3-link-on-carecontext#m2-linking-care-context-call-back","id":"hiecm.callback.m2-linking-care-context-call-back","summary":"ABDM answers a care context link request on the HIP's bridge with the outcome.","title":"Linking care context Call back API","type":"callback"},{"doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/api/m2/endpoints/m2-consent-management-data-flow-hip/01-m2-post-consent-v3-request-hip-on-notify#m2-consent-hip-on-notify","id":"hiecm.endpoint.m2-consent-hip-on-notify","summary":"The HIP acknowledges a consent granted, revoked or expired notification, one consent artefact at a time.","title":"Acknowledge a consent notification","type":"endpoint"},{"doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/api/m2/errors#abdm-1026","id":"hiecm.error.abdm-1026","summary":"The link token you sent cannot authorise this link, so generate a new one rather than retrying.","title":"ABDM-1026, the link token is not valid","type":"error"}]}
{"catalogue_version":"2026.09.16","hits":[{"doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/concepts/care-context#care-context","id":"hiecm.concept.care-context","summary":"A care context is the unit a provider links to a patient's ABHA address, carrying a reference number and a display name and nothing clinical.","title":"Care contexts, how records are grouped so they can be found","type":"concept"},{"doc_url":"","id":"hiecm.concept.m2-inbound-is-a-surface","summary":"ABDM asks your bridge questions and waits, most of them carry no documented payload, and a handler that only logs leaves records undiscoverable.","title":"Inbound is a surface, and silence there is a failure state","type":"concept"},{"doc_url":"","id":"hiecm.concept.m2-exchange-not-call","summary":"Every linking call answers twice, so group the outbound call, the wait and the callback into one row keyed by request id.","title":"The unit of work is an exchange, not a call","type":"concept"},{"doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/concepts/gateway#asynchronous-callbacks","id":"hiecm.concept.asynchronous-callbacks","summary":"Most HIE-CM calls answer 202 at once and deliver the real answer later as a callback to your registered URL, matched by request id.","title":"Asynchronous calls and callbacks, why a 200 means very little","type":"concept"},{"doc_url":"","id":"hiecm.concept.m2-never-block-the-desk","summary":"Linking answers on a callback that may be a minute away or may never come, so start the work, return at once, and keep where it got to on the record.","title":"Nobody is standing there, so never block and never lose the state","type":"concept"}]}
